WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.310
In 1995, Japan had about 86.9
million people of working age.

2
00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:11.170
By 2024, the number
was about 73.7 million.

3
00:00:11.170 --> 00:00:13.510
Around 15 per cent fewer.

4
00:00:13.510 --> 00:00:17.390
Does a shrinking workforce have
to mean a shrinking economy?

5
00:00:17.390 --> 00:00:20.620
What really sets the most
a country can produce?

6
00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:23.240
And if people and firms simply spend more,

7
00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:25.790
can output rise beyond that limit?

8
00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:28.480
In this mission, you'll
compare two views of how

9
00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:30.650
an economy's supply behaves.

10
00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:34.260
Then you'll test both views
for yourself in a graph lab.

11
00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:37.660
Your mission: find out what
sets a country's limit,

12
00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:39.550
and whether spending can break it.
